@startuml ai-sdlc-hooks
title ai-sdlc — the four PreToolUse hooks (exact deny rules)
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam wrapWidth 300

start
:tool call intercepted (PreToolUse);
:hook sources _root.sh then _hook.sh
exec form ("command":"bash","args":[...]), 10 s timeout;
if (sdlc.config.json at repo root?) then (no)
  :exit 0 silently
  (evals/cases/hooks-silent.sh asserts this);<<#C8E6C9>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

note right
  Path lists are read with hook_list:
  key absent  => built-in defaults
  key == []   => nothing (home list stays)
  key == list => replaces the defaults
  Matching: gitignore-style scripts/_glob.sh
end note

:== guard-secrets ==
Read, Glob, Grep, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit, Bash, PowerShell;
if (path or extracted shell token matches\n.env / .env.* (except .env.example, .env.sample, .env.template, .env.dist),\nsecrets/**, *-key.pem, *.key.pem, privkey.pem, *.key,\nid_rsa, id_ed25519, id_ecdsa, *.p12, *.pfx,\ncredentials.json, service-account*.json,\n~/.ssh ~/.aws ~/.azure ~/.config/gh ~/.kube/config ~/.netrc ~/.npmrc ~/.docker/config.json\nOR a read-or-copy command mentioning GITHUB_TOKEN= GH_TOKEN=\nAZURE_DEVOPS_EXT_PAT= AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE .netrc\nor a whole private key name?) then (yes)
  :exit 2 — deny, reason on stderr naming the fix;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
note right
  guardrails.secretPaths replaces the project
  defaults and is applied literally (no exemption);
  [] leaves only the home list.
  cert.pem, fullchain.pem, *.crt and *.pub are
  not secrets — readable.
  .claude/settings.json deny rules carry the
  same names as a second layer.
end note

:== guard-protected-paths ==
Edit, Write, NotebookEdit, Bash, PowerShell;
if (modifies .sdlc/UNLOCK_PROTECTED or .sdlc/release/** ?) then (yes)
  :exit 2 — always denied, the markers never unlock themselves,
  so the agent can neither create the unlock marker nor write
  a release authorisation;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (modifies a path in guardrails.protectedPaths\n(nothing by default)?) then (yes)
  if (.sdlc/UNLOCK_PROTECTED exists (human-written)?) then (yes)
    :allow this one edit;
  else (no)
    :exit 2 — deny, reads stay allowed;<<#FFCDD2>>
    stop
  endif
else (no)
endif

:== guard-verifier-readonly ==
Edit, Write, NotebookEdit;
if (agent_type is sdlc-verifier or sdlc-security-auditor\n(with or without a plugin prefix)?) then (yes)
  :exit 2 — every file edit denied. Their shell is NOT restricted,
  report-don't-fix lives in the agent prompt, and a PASS must
  state the verified tree;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif

:== gate-production ==
Bash, PowerShell;
if (command matches environments.prod.deployCommandPatterns?\nglobs anchored on shell separators, no built-in patterns —\ninit seeds "git push * <default branch>" plus\ncommands.deployProduction (exact and <cmd>*)) then (no match / empty list)
  :nothing gated;
else (match)
  :read .sdlc/release/AUTHORIZED-<HEAD sha>,
  validate with scripts/ship/_authz.sh;
  if (authorised_by=, authorised_at=, expires= (digits, strictly future)\nand commit= (full sha == HEAD == file name),\neach present exactly once?) then (no)
    :exit 2 — deny with the specific reason,
    message: run /ai-sdlc:sdlc-ship;<<#FFCDD2>>
    stop
  else (yes)
    :allow this command until the marker expires;
  endif
endif

:exit 0 — the tool call proceeds;<<#C8E6C9>>
note right
  Not gated: source, tests, lockfiles, CI files,
  sdlc.config.json, .claude/settings.json, installs,
  scripts, staging deploys. Format, lint and verify are
  the agent's job after a coherent change, not a hook.
  No shell classifier: path-like tokens plus a broad
  "can this write" regex (hook_cmd_writes) plus the
  configured globs, so `npm test && git push origin main`
  is still caught.
end note
stop
@enduml
